{"type":"standard","title":"Mark Warner","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mark Warner</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q453893","titles":{"canonical":"Mark_Warner","normalized":"Mark Warner","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mark Warner</span></span>"},"pageid":13295044,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Mark_Warner_2025.jpg/330px-Mark_Warner_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":412},"originalimage":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Mark_Warner_2025.jpg/3840px-Mark_Warner_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":4766,"height":5957},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1371700151","tid":"a0074ca5-a272-11f1-993b-6276dd5c532d","timestamp":"2026-08-27T23:54:22Z","description":"American politician (born 1954)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Warner","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Warner?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Warner?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mark_Warner"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Warner","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Mark_Warner","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Warner?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mark_Warner"}},"extract":"Mark Robert Warner is an American businessman and politician serving as the senior United States senator from Virginia, a seat he has held since 2009. A member of the Democratic Party, Warner served as the 69th governor of Virginia from 2002 to 2006. He is vice chair of the Senate Democratic Caucus and vice chair of the Senate Intelligence Committee.","extract_html":"<p><b>Mark Robert Warner</b> is an American businessman and politician serving as the senior United States senator from Virginia, a seat he has held since 2009. A member of the Democratic Party, Warner served as the 69th governor of Virginia from 2002 to 2006. He is vice chair of the Senate Democratic Caucus and vice chair of the Senate Intelligence Committee.</p>"}